1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,920
Two more for us, huh?

2
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:25,760
Oh, there's a good boy.

3
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,120
Here you go.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,320
I was starting to think you would never calm down.

5
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,180
Are you brothers?

6
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:43,360
Same age, so possibly twins as well.

7
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:45,180
No, they're neither.

8
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:48,060
This one here is sweet and well-behaved.

9
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:51,280
And this one, well, he's a bit spirited.

10
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:56,480
Then there's the fact that they don't look a thing alike.

11
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,520
Hmm, you know.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,320
Hmm, now, for this spirited little thing...

13
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:05,520
Ow!

14
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:09,580
Ow, a bit too spirited.

15
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,100
Asta, huh?

16
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:22,340
Well, you've had a tough beginning, but your worries are over.

17
00:01:22,340 --> 00:01:25,460
As of today, boys, this will be your home.

18
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,040
Asta and Yuno.

19
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:45,300
With all this work, I sure hope we have a good harvest.

20
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:47,180
Yeah, same here.

21
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:53,700
What's that about?

22
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,940
That kid from the church is at it again.

23
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:58,140
One day, I'll be the Wizard King!

24
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,720
And I'll make you the happiest woman in the world!

25
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:04,620
That's why I'm asking, will you please marry me?

26
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:06,360
I'm sorry, Asta.

27
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:07,720
I just can't.

28
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:09,320
It's my duty to serve everyone.

29
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,100
That's a no!

30
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,300
Yes, it is.

31
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:15,740
I can't marry you.

32
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:18,620
I'm not giving up yet!

33
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,300
You should, really.

34
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,220
Please, Asta.

35
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,340
Not giving up!

36
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,620
I'm truly sorry!

37
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:27,000
Please, Sister Lily, just let me ask one more time!

38
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:28,600
No!

39
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:36,080
Water creation magic is my best of love!

40
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,560
I'm so sorry, Asta.

41
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:41,020
I wasn't thinking.

42
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:42,760
My magic just slipped out.

43
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:45,680
Nice, Sister.

44
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:46,480
Way to go.

45
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:48,120
Show him no mercy.

46
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:51,160
But I didn't mean to.

47
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:53,100
We're not done here!

48
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:59,920
Come on.

49
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:03,540
How many times does she have to turn you down?

50
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:07,220
Why are you sticking your nose in this, Yuno?

51
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:10,640
That's simple, really.

52
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,240
Because you're noisy, you're short.

53
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,700
You lack both composure and tolerance.

54
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,200
And there's not really anything about you that appeals to women.

55
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:21,420
Hey!

56
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:24,980
Fifteen years of growing up together and that's how you talk to me?

57
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:26,720
You big lady killing jerk!

58
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:28,240
May I help?

59
00:03:28,340 --> 00:03:29,060
Thank you, Yuno.

60
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:31,160
You think you can just ignore me?

61
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,040
Asta.

62
00:03:33,840 --> 00:03:36,560
Nuns are women of the cloth, which means they can't marry.

63
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,080
Neither can fifteen-year-old boys, in fact.

64
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,340
Think you're so smart.

65
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:42,440
Well, I'll show you.

66
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:44,220
Yeah, I will.

67
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:46,940
You and me, right here, right now!

68
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,040
Not today.

69
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:49,580
And why the hell not, huh?

70
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:52,260
It'll be a waste of time.

71
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,440
What'd you say to me?

72
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:55,740
Give it a rest already, Yasta.

73
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:58,600
There's no way you stand a chance against him and you know it.

74
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:00,080
Take this!

75
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:01,260
And...

76
00:04:01,260 --> 00:04:04,000
This is pointless.

77
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:04,620
Kill!

78
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,740
You know that you can't use magic.

79
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,160
Oh, what?

80
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:09,100
Come on!

81
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:12,100
Still nothing?

82
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:12,800
Why?

83
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,680
You're funny, Yasta!

84
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:16,500
It is pretty crazy.

85
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:19,740
Not being able to use any kind of magic at his age?

86
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:20,900
That never happens.

87
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:22,560
What's your deal, huh?

88
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,780
I'm older than you, kid!

89
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:24,660
Show some respect!

90
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:25,840
Not a chance.

91
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:28,840
Haven't you figured out that in this world, magic is everything?

92
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:31,700
It's not a matter of whether you have it, but how much.

93
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:35,560
You're the only person I've ever heard of who can't use any magic at all.

94
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:39,220
All right, then.

95
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:42,620
Looks like I'm gonna have to bust out my secret moves.

96
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:45,280
You've got secret moves?

97
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:49,520
Bet you can't do crunches this fast!

98
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:52,560
Like anyone cares, idiot.

99
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:54,600
I'm just getting money again!

100
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:02,100
Look at that!

101
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,520
You look amazing!

102
00:05:03,540 --> 00:05:04,820
This is nothing for him.

103
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,320
Such a big help, thank you.

104
00:05:10,980 --> 00:05:11,820
All right!

105
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:14,300
Leave the wood chopping to me!

106
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,720
I've got this covered!

107
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:20,280
Oh, jeez.

108
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:21,720
They're really the same age?

109
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,140
You definitely can't tell it from the way they act.

110
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,900
Yuno is the hope of this church!

111
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:34,700
Getting into the magic knights isn't just a silly dream for Yuno.

112
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,200
He'll make it for sure.

113
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:39,460
The awarding of the grimoires is coming up.

114
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:41,480
Once you have yours, things will change.

115
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:42,640
Just wait and see, Asta.

116
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:45,120
You'll be able to use magic in no time at all.

117
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:47,980
Thank you so much, Sister Lily.

118
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:49,400
Well, probably anyway.

119
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:51,580
My grimoire.

120
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,520
I'll have it soon.

121
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:55,020
Finally.

122
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:56,620
Finally.

123
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:57,840
That's right!

124
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,140
I'm going to get the most awesome grimoire ever!

125
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:01,940
I'll join up with the magic knights,

126
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,720
and once I make a name for myself,

127
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:06,680
I'll follow in your footsteps and become the wizard king!

128
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:09,120
He'll never give up this nonsense, will he?

129
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:12,640
And then I'll come back and rebuild this crumbling dump of a church!

130
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:15,240
Crumbling dump!

131
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,680
That's taking it too far!

132
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:18,020
Isn't that right, Yuno?

133
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,020
Huh?

134
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,480
I'll show all of you.

135
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:36,440
I swear, just watch and you'll see, damn you!

136
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:37,840
Asta, wait!

137
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,300
Really?

138
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,060
How am I younger than him?

139
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,080
Hey, Yuno?

140
00:06:51,860 --> 00:06:55,120
Do you think you could maybe try to get along a little better with Asta?

141
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:59,160
I mean, like you used to back when you were younger.

142
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:00,900
You two were always together.

143
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:03,360
Yuno used to be such a crybaby.

144
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,400
But then one day,

145
00:07:05,980 --> 00:07:07,200
he came back with Asta,

146
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:08,520
who was badly injured.

147
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,320
And since then,

148
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:12,740
I haven't seen him cry once.

149
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:15,420
What's the point?

150
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:17,500
There's no getting along with that one.

151
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:20,760
Now that I think about it,

152
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:22,620
they were both different afterwards.

153
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:26,300
That's when Asta started coming home covered in mud every day.

154
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:29,200
I wonder where he goes off to and what he's doing.

155
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:31,120
994,

156
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:32,920
995,

157
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:34,760
996,

158
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,460
997,

159
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:38,220
998,

160
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:39,820
999!

161
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:46,420
And now for some magic-enhancing mogul leaf juice.

162
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:47,280
Bottoms up!

163
00:07:47,280 --> 00:08:00,900
I will be the Wizard King.

164
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,120
Nothing's going to stop me.

165
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:07,640
And the first step is getting my body trained up!

166
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:08,600
March.

167
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:19,340
When the Firefly Dandelions float through the air,

168
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:21,580
once a year throughout the Clover Kingdom,

169
00:08:21,820 --> 00:08:24,340
those children who have reached 15 years of age

170
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:26,640
gather for the Grimoire Acceptance Ceremony,

171
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:30,340
a rite of passage that will increase their magical power.

172
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:31,600
Awesome!

173
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:34,260
Are all these shelves filled with Grimoires?

174
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,480
Which one is mine?

175
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,800
Once I get my hands on a Grimoire,

176
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:41,680
I'm going to be able to use magic too.

177
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,260
I'll catch up to you soon enough, you know.

178
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:46,700
Hmm.

179
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:50,100
The day that I'll become a full-fledged mage,

180
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:51,020
it's about time.

181
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,540
Look what the cat dragged in.

182
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:54,600
Could they be any shabbier?

183
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:56,920
We shouldn't have to give Grimoires to anyone

184
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:58,480
who just walks in off the street.

185
00:08:58,820 --> 00:09:00,220
Makes me sick to my stomach.

186
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:02,240
You don't think the pathetic creatures

187
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,520
would be foolish enough to attempt

188
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:06,000
the Magic Knight's entrance exam in six months, do you?

189
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:08,740
Only high-ranking nobles and royalty

190
00:09:08,740 --> 00:09:11,560
have enough innate magic power to pass the exam.

191
00:09:11,920 --> 00:09:13,100
See the shrimpy one?

192
00:09:13,660 --> 00:09:15,760
I heard that he can't use magic at all.

193
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:16,960
Oh, wow.

194
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:19,760
We'd better take extra special care of him.

195
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,580
I mean, he's one of a kind.

196
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:23,900
The only person in the entire country

197
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:25,180
who can't use magic.

198
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:28,960
Welcome to Grimoire Tower,

199
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,060
except he's.

200
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:31,600
On this momentous day,

201
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:34,320
you will take your first step down a new path.

202
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:37,620
I wish you integrity, hope, and love.

203
00:09:39,620 --> 00:09:41,180
For those who don't know,

204
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:43,600
I am the master of this Grimoire Tower.

205
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:47,000
Now, never once has anyone from this region

206
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,920
distinguished him or herself

207
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:50,600
by becoming a magic knight,

208
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:52,320
much less the wizard king.

209
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,420
I pray that one among you

210
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:55,440
will have what it takes

211
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:57,880
to become the most powerful mage in the land.

212
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:00,500
Seriously, I mean it!

213
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,100
And now,

214
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:05,640
to accept

215
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:08,260
your Grimoires.

216
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:21,400
Finally,

217
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:22,920
my very own Grimoire.

218
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:23,940
Check it out.

219
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:25,180
Mine's bigger than yours.

220
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:25,980
Yeah, maybe,

221
00:10:26,100 --> 00:10:26,960
but mine's thicker.

222
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,080
Here it is.

223
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:30,040
My one-way ticket

224
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,340
out of this little village.

225
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:32,740
I could carry on

226
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:33,760
the family business.

227
00:10:34,580 --> 00:10:36,140
But this is my Grimoire?

228
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:37,060
Seriously?

229
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:38,900
Why is mine so tiny?

230
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:41,860
I guess

231
00:10:41,860 --> 00:10:43,660
I'll decide what to do

232
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:45,640
once there are more pages of magic in here.

233
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:48,720
Six months from now,

234
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:49,300
we'll be taking

235
00:10:49,300 --> 00:10:51,540
the prestigious magic knight's entrance exam.

236
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:53,060
And we'll pass it, too.

237
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:53,700
Just wait.

238
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,780
Yes, very good.

239
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:58,260
I have high hopes for you.

240
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,140
Hey, uh...

241
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:06,740
Is my Grimoire

242
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:07,460
